{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"versicolor-needless-jackal","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOnce the legacy `reconcile` CLI route and its `--filter-local-ids` flag are removed (by seagreen-wet-bluefish / 82bb-439b-1c42-4abd), the legacy route is the ONLY producer of a non-None `ctx.filter_local_ids`. `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py:95` documents it: \"--filter-local-ids is available only on the legacy route.\" After that removal the internal `filter_local_ids` field defaults to `None` everywhere, so every `selection_ids or filter_local_ids` fallback collapses to `selection_ids` and every `if filter_local_ids:` branch is dead.\n\nThis ticket removes that now-dead engine plumbing (a pure simplification, no behavior change), kept SEPARATE from 82bb to keep the CLI-removal change bounded and reviewable.\n\n## Scope\n\nRemove the always-None `filter_local_ids` parameter/field and its dead branches from the reconciler engine, threading through only where it was a real input:\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py` (field + param)\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_phase.py` (post-filter branch + `_build_filter_target_set` call)\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/load_phase.py`, `outbound_pass.py`, `run_differs.py`, `snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` (`selection_ids or filter_local_ids` fallbacks collapse to `selection_ids`)\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/persist_phase.py` (result[\"filter_local_ids\"] emission)\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/pass_support.py` (`_build_filter_target_set` helper, if unused elsewhere)\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py` / `request.py` (residual internal field, after 82bb removes the flag)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `filter_local_ids` is fully removed from the reconciler engine; no `selection_ids or filter_local_ids` fallbacks or `if filter_local_ids:` branches remain.\n- [ ] The canonical `--only`/`--except` selection (`selection_ids`) path is unchanged and proven by existing scoped-pass tests.\n- [ ] No change to any persisted state, exit code, or reconcile result contract.\n\n## Depends on\n\nMust land AFTER 82bb (seagreen-wet-bluefish) removes the legacy reconcile CLI route + `--filter-local-ids` flag.","id":"f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0","parent_id":"0cfc-e511-8f8a-4c8b","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove dead filter_local_ids engine plumbing after legacy reconcile route removal"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788483637431525604,"uuid":"adfae486-d3d1-46b9-b5f8-afa833ec3c61"}